---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout 
  title="About — Noha Khaled"
  description="Analytics engineer with 7+ years of engineering problem-solving experience. I build 
  reliable pipelines, data models, and reporting from messy, technical data."
  >
  
  <!-- Changed max-w-3xl to max-w-5xl to match the rest of the site -->
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    
    <!-- Page Header -->
    <header class="mb-16">
      <h1 class="text-5xl md:text-7xl font-display font-bold tracking-tighter text-onyx mb-6">
        About
      </h1>
      <!-- Changed to text-dim and matched size to Work page -->
       <!-- 
      <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-dim leading-relaxed">
        I spent seven years solving engineering problems. Now I solve data problems the same way: understand the system, find where it breaks, fix it properly.
      </p>
       -->
    </header>

    <!-- Content Sections -->
    <!-- Restricted width to max-w-3xl so the reading experience stays comfortable -->
    <div class="space-y-16 text-lg text-dim leading-relaxed">
      
      <!-- Section 1 -->
      <section>
        <p>
          Mechanical engineer by training. Seven years in simulation and CFD. Lead technical analyst by the end. Now building analytics systems — pipelines, data models, and reporting. 
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-semibold text-onyx mb-4 tracking-tight">How I got here</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Graduated from Mechanical Engineering, Cairo University, Class of 2018.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4">
          I worked at Optumatics from 2018 to its closure mid 2026, working on thermal and fluid modelling of vehicle parts, validating simulation results against real-world data, 
          and presenting findings and design recommendations to the client. </p>
        <p class = "mb-4">
          Over time the work shifted from running simulations to leading people 
          and processes - training a team of 15 engineers and building processes that made the team less dependent on me.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4">
          I gravitated over the years towards data. Simulations produce enormous amounts of it across files and systems, 
          and most of the hard work was shaping it so that anyone could ask a question of it. And I built that needed system. 
        </p>
        <p>
          Post Optumatics's closure, I kept going. I rebuilt the pipeline as a public project <a href="/work/case-engineering-pipeline" class="italic hover:text-accent"> (check it here)</a>, taught myself the modern data stack, 
          and started building things end to end to understand how tools and software fit together.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-semibold text-onyx mb-4 tracking-tight">How I learn</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          With curiosity-driven structure.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4"> 
          I learn by building what I need, hitting a wall, then reading and researching until I understand the wall. This way, I can create a mental model of tools and concepts,
          backed up by what I experienced first-hand. And I always utilize AI (mostly DeepSeek & Claude) as a personal readily available teacher.
        </p>

        <p class="mb-4">
          I also like to regularly remind myself of Richard Feynman's famous saying:
        </p>
            <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-accent bg-accent/5 p-6 rounded-r-lg">
              <p class="text-base md:text-lg text-dim font-medium leading-relaxed">
                "Study hard what interests you the most in the most undisciplined, irreverent and original manner possible."
              </p>
            </blockquote>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-semibold text-onyx mb-4 tracking-tight">How I work with people</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          I've led a team of 15 engineers: training them, evaluating them, and building processes so the team got more autonomous over time.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4">
          I've also handled client communication directly, negotiated deliverables, and presented simulation findings with design recommendations to stakeholders.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 5 -->
      <section id="what-im-looking-for" class="scroll-mt-32">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-semibold text-onyx mb-4 tracking-tight">What I'm looking for</h2>
        <p class="mb-2">
          Full-time/Part-time/Contract Analytics Engineer or Data Analyst roles. <br>
          Fully remote, locally or internationally. <br>
          Hybrid locally. I'll consider fully onsite for the right offer.
        </p>
        <!-- 
        <p class="mb-4 text-onyx italic">
          <br>I'm currently between roles and available immediately.
        </p>
         -->
      </section>

      <!-- Section 6 -->
      <section class="pt-8 border-t border-border">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-semibold text-onyx mb-4 tracking-tight">Off the clock</h2>
        <p>
          I love making things with my hands; I got into carpentry for a while, and I paint and draw regularly. <br>
          I practice yoga sometimes, and I've swum twice a week for about a year now 🏊🏼.<br>
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>